Designed three custom instructions to accelerate CRC-64-ECMA, CRC-32, and CRC-16 computations. Based on historical reviewers' feedback and strict core constraints (specifically that wide input blocks imply a large internal area cost), the instructions process 4 to 8 bytes per invocation (requiring just a 3-word block wrapper) instead of large 64-byte blocks. This avoids massive area bloat while still delivering excellent performance by reducing the instruction issue and memory movement overheads per byte. The instructions safely compute bit-by-bit CRCs in a constant-time manner internally, zero out all unused output block words to prevent residue leaks, and stay strictly within their specified bounds without arbitrary pointer dereferences.